I’m choosing a countdown implementation with two real `while` loops. It stays within the translator’s supported integer/Boolean subset, handles every Python integer (non-positive inputs return `0`, matching `range(n)`), and exposes clean proof cutpoints: the inner loop counts `7` digits of one number; the outer loop accumulates qualifying numbers below `n`.
